e relay at Croydon Arena. For full details of the occasion see page 13.","id":"B170-01","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B194/B194-p14-flashback-southern-1939.jpg","c":"Charlie Smart leads the 3 miles field in the Southern Counties A.A.A. Championships of 1939 at Motspur Park. Tom Carter (No. 32) lies 4th with Ted Stimpson (No. 25) 9th.","id":"B194-28","w":"April 1977"},{"f":"crops/B208/B208-p06-walking-section.jpg","c":"The Walking Section congratulate Joe Coleman following his election to the President's office. L to R; Back row. Carl Lawton, Mike Scamell, John Keown John Newman, Russell Day, John Dunsford. Middle. John Morris, Fred Denny, Richard Dorman, JOE COLEMAN, John Llewellin,Ed. Crossingham, Tom Carter, Ted Stimpson, Kneeling; Graham Seatter, Ron Day, John Hall.","id":"B208-12","w":"October 1984"},{"f":"crops/B211/B211-p44-back-cover-lucas-internationals.jpg","c":"President Bill Lucas poses with four of our surviving England Cross Country Internationals Arthur Penny(1933/34/39),C.T.Carter(1936),E.S,Stimpson(1939) and V.Blowfield(1948).","id":"B211-79","w":"June 1987"},{"f":"crops/B219/B219-p08-stimpson-relay.jpg","c":"Vern Blowfield hands the baton over to Ted who sets off on the second leg of the \"News of the World\" London to Brighton Relay held on April 19th 1947. The Bels went on to win by over two minutes.\n(Editor's note: Actually we have stuck our necks out here, for the same combination of runners were also involved in the first take-over in April 1950, with Ted \"running a blinder\". No doubt someone will correct us if necessary).","id":"B219-21","w":"November 1992"},{"f":"crops/B164/B164-p01-ted-stimpson-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER (Photo:E.D.Lacey)----Our President for 1967/8, TED STIMPSON.","id":"B164-01","w":"December 1967"},{"f":"crops/B169/B169-p18-downbeat-poll-stimpson.jpg","c":"DOWNBEAT POLL","id":"B169-47","w":"March 1969"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B164/B164-p01-ted-stimpson-cover.jpg","caption":"FRONT COVER (Photo:E.D.Lacey)----Our President for 1967/8, TED STIMPSON.","source":"B164-01","when":"December 1967"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Ted Stimpson in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1934–2003: 183 mentions in 80 issues, 92 race results and 9 photographs. Wrote or reported 5 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B169/B169-p18-downbeat-poll-stimpson.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-ted-stimpson.html"},"legend":false}